  "body": "## Description\n\nThe trusted-entities statement generated for the Lambda execution role cannot currently carry IAM conditions.\n\n`assume_role_policy_statements` does support conditions, but it *appends* statements to the same policy document. IAM trust policies OR across statements, so an added conditioned statement does not restrict the unconditioned service principal — it only widens the trust.\n\nThat leaves no way to apply confused-deputy protections such as `aws:SourceAccount` while still using the module's role management. The only workaround today is `create_role = false` plus a hand-built role passed as `lambda_role`, which forfeits the module's CloudWatch Logs, VPC, tracing and DLQ policy attachments.\n\nThis adds an `assume_role_conditions` variable applied to the existing trusted-entities statement.\n\n## Motivation and Context\n\nSecurity scanners flag the default trust as a confused-deputy risk — Prowler reports it as `iam_role_cross_service_confused_deputy_prevention`, and AWS' own guidance recommends `aws:SourceAccount`/`aws:SourceArn` on service trust relationships.\n\nIn an estate of a few hundred functions this is a single module default repeated everywhere, so it is not practically fixable per-function without abandoning the module.\n\n`aws:SourceAccount` is the more useful of the two conditions here: `aws:SourceArn` pins each role to a specific function name and breaks on rename, whereas the account condition is uniform across every function.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\nNone. `assume_role_conditions` defaults to `[]`, which produces byte-identical output to the current behaviour for existing users.\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n- `pre-commit run terraform_fmt`, `terraform_validate`, `end-of-file-fixer`, `trailing-whitespace` — all pass\n- `README.md` inputs table updated for the new variable\n- Verified that with the default `[]` the generated trust policy is unchanged, and that supplying a condition produces:\n\n```hcl\nassume_role_conditions = [{\n  test     = \"StringEquals\"\n  variable = \"aws:SourceAccount\"\n  values   = [data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id]\n}]\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n  \"Action\": \"sts:AssumeRole\",\n  \"Principal\": { \"Service\": \"lambda.amazonaws.com\" },\n  \"Condition\": { \"StringEquals\": { \"aws:SourceAccount\": \"123456789012\" } }\n}\n```\n\nHappy to add an `examples/` entry if you'd prefer one for this.\n",
